/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:16:role              = "face-proof — how a session proves ONE face at a gate without naming its vessel, under the PER-VESSEL shape: the face proof key per (PersonaGroup, Nexus) stays with the root-holding vessel and no private face key travels; each joined vessel mints its own face-scoped key, certified once at the join; a session signer chains beneath it. The gate reads face key → vessel's face-scoped key → session key, under one Nexus admit per face. Carries the key hierarchy, the gate exchange (a minimal Noise IK first flight in the WebSocket subprotocol token, provisional work only, a signed finish before any verdict), what the gate, a herm, a co-member and an observer each learn, the named leaks, causal deny-only withdrawal, the sibling channel's move to face scope, and what an offline root holder means"
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:32:''Why this stands as its own carrier, beside the session contract.'' The session contract (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract">>) governs the inside of one vessel: its owner, its islands, its holder. This carrier governs the wire: a gate, a herm, a sibling and an observer read it, and none of them reads the holder's protocol. The two meet at one field, the session's proof subject, and each builds on its own order.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:34:> ''Register.'' The operator ruled the browser's first proof (operator ruling, 2026-10-11; quote license: //"Approve your lean on the browser first-proof carrier."//). The per-vessel custody shape stands adopted by the house under the operator's standing grant; the operator read it and overruled nothing. The remainder reads as ''the designed shape''. #/owed names what stays unproven, and a builder MUST NOT harden an unproven part into code as law.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:49:| Herm relay identity | the dialer mints a separate fresh signer for each herm dial | one dial's memory | the herm sees this key and a face-scoped channel tag |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:50:| Gate bundle | the gate derives separate, domain-separated transport and signing keys per (tier, Nexus, route): a floor route's from the floor key, a serving route's from the serving key, a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (#/the-gate-exchange) | nowhere: a bundle lives in memory from a derivation to a drop; a dialer pins it per (Nexus, route) | the dialer, and anyone handed the pin |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:52:''The face's lineage re-issues the face proof key.'' The standing key and a successor minted at random both sign one hand-over; the record rides the Nexus's carriage board, the admit keeps naming the key the Nexus admitted, and a gate reads that key's line, stands a presenter under its head alone, and reads a line that forks as denied. A kapae on any key of the line holds the whole line. A gate that has not yet read the hand-over still stands the key it handed on, and no shared moment closes that gap; a compromise of the key therefore takes the face-key roll (#/causal-withdrawal), never a hand-over. A Handle card names its handle-KEL prefix, which no per-Nexus key enters, so a hand-over moves no card (house reading).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:66:''The admit proves Nexus standing; the private face grant proves PersonaGroup capability. Neither substitutes for the other.'' A gate outside the PersonaGroup needs the Nexus admit alone. A gate that shares PersonaGroup planes also asks the ring to verify the private, root-authorized grant against that face's event history. No root edge rides beside the leaf (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/two-maps">>).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:76:The dialer pins the gate bundle before it dials. Every signature uses its own domain bytes and a canonical field encoding.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:78:# ''The first flight.'' A browser's upgrade request carries the knock in its URL path and a ''minimal'' Noise IK message 1 as a token in `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol`, beside one fixed application protocol name. A node dialer rides the same upgrade, knock path and subprotocol token through its `ws` client (`nodeDialSocket` over `wsDialSocket`): one upgrade on both hosts.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:79:# ''The gate answers the upgrade only after that flight decrypts.'' A flight that decrypts shows the dialer knows the gate's pinned key, which silence toward strangers protects. The gate then sends its 101 and selects the fixed protocol name alone. A wrong knock or a flight that fails to decrypt draws no answer.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:82:# ''The presentation follows in the first encrypted frames.'' A face's presentation carries the face's public key, the vessel's face-scoped key with its certificate, the session key with its certificate, ONE presentation arm (an admit, a hosting grant, or an invite claim) and that arm's causal lineage, and the presenter's withdrawal frontier with any events the gate may lack (#/the-withdrawal-proof). An admit's `nym` MUST equal the face key. No ContactCard, no vessel key, no persona root, no root edge, no identifier shared across faces, and by default no Handle rides it.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:84:''The admit's signed bytes carry the canon-document list and a validated full `GateBundlePin` for the hearth's sovereign sync route at its named Nexus. `readGateBundlePin` reads the object and its digest derives from it; the quorum's salted `carriageCommit` binds the opening inside the act image. A joinee reads the opening only through the admit at its held root (`verifySignedAdmitBundle`). Floor routes receive separate full pins through an authenticated relation or signed pin set; a floor announcement cannot authenticate its own first pin. `device-admit.ts` mints the internal `device-admit/v1` edge, and the fleet answer carries the pin and canon list.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:86:# ''The gate checks, still provisionally.'' It checks the pinned route and audience, the chain, the presentation's signatures, the quorum's signatures, the causal parents, the deny events and withdrawals it has learned (#/causal-withdrawal), and the roll anchors. Where the asked planes need it, the ring checks the PersonaGroup grant. Missing required history, a known fork or an incomplete board brings abstention. The gate reveals no differentiated refusal.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:89:# ''Both ends close the dial'' and discard its transport and herm-dial keys. The daemon drops the session signer when its session ends or switches.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:95:* ''The knock derives from the bundle's digest'', and the handshake's prologue holds that digest. So a gate's knock, its pin, its verdict and its posture all read per Nexus exactly, and a first flight decrypts only at the gate whose pin its dialer held.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:105:* ''Whether a hosting grant or an invite claim holds stays the sorter's own reading.'' The gate binds the arm to the face key and the Nexus, and attaches a walker only where the sorter read one.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:110:!!! The tiers of gate ~ the floor answers locked, the sovereign gate answers raised, the serving gate answers an ember's raise
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:114:''A route names its tier, and a tier names its root.'' A ''floor route'' answers at a locked vessel: the public shelf, the oracle's read face, the floor's announcement, and a herm's blind relay of bytes it cannot open. Its bundle derives from the floor key. A ''sovereign route'' seats a face's session, syncs a private document or serves a lane whose bytes this vessel can open. Its bundle derives from the sealed custody root, and it exists only while the vessel stands unlocked. A route's typed name carries its tier, the pin states it and the pin's digest binds it: no route asks the other tier's root, a root asked for the wrong tier refuses by name, and a dialer that pinned one tier believes no gate of the other.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:116:''Each derivation takes the tier, the Nexus and the route under its own name.'' No pin, key, digest or knock of one tier, one Nexus or one route links to another for an outsider: one vessel's floor pin and its sovereign pin for one Nexus share nothing.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:118:''A dialer names the tier it means to reach'', and a pin of another tier dials nothing: a floor gate's `verified` seats the floor alone, so no caller mistakes it for a sovereign seat.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:120:''What each tier costs.'' A thief who holds the disk and no passphrase holds the floor key: that thief can stand the floor gates, and can speak as the PLACE wherever the place's own key speaks (its carrier seal, a place arm), which reaches the public floor and the blind carriage of bytes it cannot open. That thief can never stand a sovereign gate, seat a face or open a sealed byte, and stands a serving gate only where the vessel's embers answer its copy (the serving tier, below).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:122:''A floor gate seats no fleet lane.'' It asks no private grant and sorts nobody same-operator, it reads no withdrawal memory and answers no refusing state, and it marks every seat it opens as the floor's, so that seat reaches the public shelf and what the floor serves, and nothing this vessel can open. A presenter that asks more dials the sovereign route, and finds no gate there while the vessel rests locked. A floor route a design adds keeps this law: the ember's route (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember#/the-raise">>) seats a dialer by the transport key a standing ember pin names, and no device of the person's fleet by its fleet key.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:124:!!! The serving tier ~ a third gate, rooted in the serving key
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:126:> ''House ruling under the operator's delegation'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings">>); it reopens on proof that a gate pin decides no authority anywhere.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:128:''A serving route answers at a vessel its embers raised to SERVING'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember">>): the serving gate for presenters already standing, and blind carriage for them. Its bundle derives from the serving key under its own registered domain, and it exists only while the vessel stands at SERVING or unlocked. The floor and sovereign tiers stand untouched: no serving route asks the floor key or the custody root, and a dialer that pinned the sovereign tier believes no serving gate. A serving gate signs its own handshake and no act, and its seat reaches what the serving tier holds and nothing beyond it.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:130:''A pin moves only by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step'', at every tier: a roll the vessel signs, a key rotation its key history verifies, or a removal a counted act carries. No quiet period ages a pin out, and no clock retires one.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:136:''A herm or a carrier holds no face'', so it holds no face key, no certificate and no session certificate. It still dials gates. The presentation therefore takes a fourth arm, the ''place arm'', and that arm stands OUTSIDE the face proof: no chain rides it and no withdrawal history answers it.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:145:* ''A place with no contract'' that dials a floor route draws what a proven stranger draws there.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:147:''Why it shares the exchange.'' One handshake keeps one silence: a place and a face meet the same knock, the same first flight, the same deadline and the same quiet, so a watcher of the wire tells neither from the other, and the socket's handshake still changes once.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:149:▢ ''OWED'': an operator's contract over their own herm (one signature, one place, one Nexus) names bytes no code holds yet; the arm reads the quorum's `carry` act until it does.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:155:!! The browser envelope ~ the first flight as an upgrade carries it
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:159:''The gate's 101 selects `lar-gate` alone'' and never echoes the token. The browser dialer reads the protocol its socket opened under and cuts any other: Chromium fails a 101 that selects nothing, while Firefox and WebKit open it under the protocol `""`, so only the dialer's own check holds the line in every engine. A foreign selection fails in all three.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:163:''What the measurement read'' (one run, a house reading of its instruments): Chromium 156, Firefox 157 and WebKit 27.2 under Playwright 1.64, over plain sockets on loopback, direct and behind `nginx:1.30-alpine` under the household terminator's own settings.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:171:| an unanswered upgrade | Firefox closes it after 20 s; Chromium and WebKit still waited at 75 s |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:172:| the terminator's log | its stock access line keeps the request path, so it keeps the knock; no line keeps the token |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:183:| The Nexus gate | the stable face key AT THAT NEXUS, so it correlates that face's sessions there (ruled acceptable: two sessions of one face may correlate); the presenting vessel's face-scoped key; the session key; the presentation and its lineage; route and audience | a vessel root key, a persona root, a root edge, or the number of vessels a face holds |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:184:| A herm | a per-dial relay key, a face-scoped channel tag, routing, locators, timing, sizes and destination; a stable tag lets it correlate ONE face's carriage | the sibling proof, document content, any certificate in the chain, or a tag two faces share |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:185:| An authorized co-member of the PersonaGroup | the private authority history, the planes its grant allows, and the certificate history, so it relates a vessel's face-scoped key to that vessel's membership | a private face key: none travels, so no co-member acts as the whole face |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:186:| An outside observer | network address, destination, timing, sizes, the clear upgrade and knock, and whatever a human discloses | the encrypted presentation |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:198:* ''A replayed first flight draws provisional work'', and tells its sender whether that flight still earns the upgrade. The signed finish still blocks every application effect.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:199:* ''A terminating proxy reads the subprotocol token and the path.'' The household terminator's stock access line keeps the path, and with it the knock, and keeps no line of the token (#/the-browser-envelope). A passive observer of an encrypted connection reads neither the path nor the header.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:200:* ''The knock tests offline'' for an observer holding candidate gate keys: a leak OPEN under roadmap row `W10`, since any pre-filter keyed on public pin material tests the same way (the reading and its measurements stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-knock-reading).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:221:> ''Register.'' The house wrote this shape under the operator's standing grant, after one round against the field's prior art: KERI's receipts and watchers, SPKI's online tests, certificate transparency and its gossip, Matrix device lists, Signal's Sesame, MLS removal and Keyhive's revocation. The whole section reads as a house reading the operator may overturn. The round found no construction that bounds an uninformed gate without a clock, a roster or an online responder, and this proof claims none.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:225:''A denial names a key by digest.'' The digest binds the face key and the Nexus, so a gate that never met the vessel learns nothing of its key, and no two histories share a value. The denial covers every certificate the face key ever signs for that key. Every denial the face key signed counts wherever a reader verified it, whether or not the reader holds the events before it. ''A withdrawn key never returns'': a vessel that joins again mints a fresh key and takes a fresh certificate (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/re-admission">>).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:227:''The frontier names how much history a party holds'': a position and the head at that position. Every presentation carries its presenter's frontier, and the signed finish covers it, so a presenter cannot later disown the frontier it showed. A presenter ahead of the gate carries the events the gate lacks.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:234:| `verified` | every signature and binding holds, the presenter's frontier meets the gate's own, and no learned denial names the key | it attaches the session, and keeps any events the presenter carried | it acts |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:235:| `unconfirmed` | the chain holds and no learned denial names the key, and the gate holds a later frontier than the presenter showed | it attaches nothing and hands over the events the presenter lacks | it acts on nothing shared, folds the events, and presents again under the later frontier |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:237:| `incomplete` | the presenter names a frontier the gate cannot join to its own: a later one with events missing, or another head at a position the gate holds | it abstains and asks for the history from its genesis | it carries the whole history |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:243:''A gate's learned state only accretes.'' Learning reads as a union of verified events, whatever order they arrive in. An older frontier never replaces a later one, a denial once counted keeps counting through a fork and after it, and a fork once proven stays proven. A presentation that carries one event the gate cannot verify teaches the gate nothing.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:269:| a withdrawn vessel that shows an older frontier | nothing at a gate that holds the denial: the denial names its key whatever frontier it claims. At a gate that never learned, the row above | the same |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:270:| a relay or a herm that withholds | nothing: the history rides inside the encrypted exchange between a presenter and the gate | |
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:279:''Two acts remove a vessel, and each answers to its own readers.'' The dyad marker sets a device aside inside its fleet: it rides the fleet's edge board, closes the sibling lane and device sync, and moves the PersonaGroup's keys (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>). The certificate withdrawal denies that vessel's face-scoped key at one Nexus's gates, and rides the face's own presentations. One removal signs the dyad raise once, and one withdrawal for each face key the vessel held a certificate under. The root-holding vessel signs both, each with one signature.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:283:* ''A standing dyad shadow with no withdrawal'' leaves the vessel shut out of its fleet and still accepted at a gate. A removal door therefore signs both acts or reports the one it could not sign.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:293:''A session opens before its certificate'' (operator ruling, approved as presented). The vessel's own chain verifies first: the face key, its certificate, this vessel's face-scoped key, with no learned denial. The face supplier joins THAT to the admit and the private grant, and the owner opens the session wearing the face. Only then does the signer mint the session's key and its certificate under the vessel's face-scoped key. The owner answers no caller between the two acts: one door opens the session and mints its signer, and a mint that fails closes the session it opened before any message routes to it. No session ever stands live with a face and no signer.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:316:''The sibling-facing proof moves to face scope together with the herm-facing stamp.'' The channel seals a face-scoped session proof and the face-private membership authority to its sibling, and binds its Repo peer id to the proven face session. It transmits no device delegation and derives no peer id from a device key. The herm stamps the separate per-dial relay identity alone.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:343:''What stands in code'': the leaf identity loads the vessel's seed and ContactCard (`packages/lararium-node/src/leaf-identity.ts`); the auth wire binds a presentation to the vessel key (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/auth-wire.ts`); the node gate sends `lar:challenge` before any proof (`packages/lararium-node/src/daemon-auth-gate.ts`); the PersonaGroup ring looks up grants by vessel key, and its own-hand path skips the check (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-group-ring.ts`); the sibling proof sends a device edge inside its sealed box (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/leaf-peer-proof.ts`).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:347:* ''The subjects'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-proof-subjects.ts`): the typed keys, the scope, the certificate and its request, the withdrawal event, the frontier, the session certificate, every signed image, and a reader for each. Every key and signature passes the one door (`ed25519-door.ts`); the purposes stand in the domain table (`domains.ts`).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:348:* ''Private authority'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-authority.ts`): minting, the request, the certificate, the withdrawal, the fold of a reader's memory, and the chain check with its six verdicts. Its callers: the fleet-join door, the removal door and the gate. It also reads a vessel's OWN chain with no session key in it (`checkVesselChain`), which a session opens on.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:350:* ''The gate bundle'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`): the floor and sovereign tiers with their typed routes and roots (the serving tier stands owed with the ember's train E), the pin, its digest, the knock, the prologue, and the transport and signing keys one gate derives per (tier, Nexus, route). Nothing rests. Its caller: the vessel's gate composer.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:352:* ''The gate'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-gate.ts`): the whole exchange against a socket and the collaborators it asks: a deadline source, an admit reader over the one presenter-verifier, the shadow ring, the grant ring, the sorter, a withdrawal memory and a session table. Every silence names ONE reason from the gate's fixed vocabulary on the vessel's own log (`GATE_SILENCE_REASONS`), with at most one detail drawn from a vocabulary the gate already types; no thrown error's text and no string a collaborator spelled reaches that log. A first flight of any length but 96 bytes draws silence before any Noise work. Its caller: the socket cutover.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:355:* ''The session face supplier'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-face.ts`): it joins a verified chain, this vessel's own key for the face, the admit's verdict and the private grant into the face a session wears, and verifies none of the last three itself (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/what-a-session-carries">>). Its callers: the same two.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:361:* ''The private grant's reader.'' The record that binds a face key to its PersonaGroup at one Nexus rests in the group's private causal state, and the ring reads it by vessel key today.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:363:* ''The floor and sovereign roots' doors'' stand at their seats (the serving key's door stands owed with train E), and no composer calls them until the socket cutover. A floor bundle asks the floor key's derive door (`vesselFloorKeyDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`), which answers while the vessel rests locked, hands back a fresh child its caller overwrites and never the floor key. A sovereign bundle asks the custody seat's (`custodyGateDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-seat.ts`), which answers only while the seat holds its key. The two doors carry two types, so a line that hands one tier's door to the other fails to compile; a root refuses a door of the other tier and a door no mint made by name (`door-other-tier`); and each seat's door refuses the other tier's child by name. A door states only what its minter claimed, so one weld holds the minters to the two seats: a second caller of either mint, anywhere in source, turns it red (`packages/lararium-node/tests/gate-root-door-minters.test.ts`). The composer owes the call.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:366:* ''The rings by face key.'' The shadow ring owes a reading over one presenter (set aside at this gate; set aside from this vessel's own fleet), and the grant ring owes the private record by face key. Both read by vessel key today.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:367:* ''The sorter over proven facts'': a class from a held admit, a private grant, the fleet reading and the arm as presented, over ONE Nexus's posture.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:372:* ''The sealed frames' layout'': the frame that carries the gate's handshake reply, and the frames that carry a presentation, a frontier and the events beside it. They ride binary WebSocket messages no proxy reads; the layout in `gate-exchange.ts` stands as the house's own; the cutover has landed, and roadmap row `W28` freezes it before the founding bake.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:373:* ''The withdrawal proof under a live partition.'' The fold and the six verdicts stand proven as pure functions over synthetic histories, and the six answers stand proven at one gate against a dialer in the same process, partitioned by hand. No two gates and no real herm have yet carried one.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:382:# ''Sibling carriage.'' The herm dial, the inner proof and the sibling peer id move to face scope.
